{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And it shall be, מדי.</b> Close to the meaning: every time the new month occurs; and similarly, מדי עברו <small>(II Kings 4:8)</small>:" "And <b>חדש בחדשו</b> is like דבר יום ביומו <small>(Exodus 5:13)</small>, and the meaning: every single day in its time. And from this verse the ancients, of blessed memory, learned that the judgment of the wicked in Gehenna is twelve months. And the meaning of מדי שנה <small>(Zechariah 14:16)</small>, [and the meaning of מדי שבת בשבתו] is in the section of seven Sabbaths <small>(Leviticus 23, 9 22, 25, 1 13)</small>:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {1 "The bracketed clause [וטעם מדי שבת בשבתו] appears to be a parenthetical insertion; the reference in parentheses lists scattered verses in Leviticus."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:20.068671058Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}